        <img src="/assets/img/NealFrancis.jpg" alt="Neal Francis - Changes">
        
        <p>
            Neal Francis arrived on the scene like a ghost from a 1970s session at Muscle Shoals. 
            His debut album, *Changes*, is a masterclass in analog soul and funk, blending 
            honky-tonk piano with a rhythmic tightness that feels both vintage and vital.
        </p>

        <p>
            Recorded to tape, the warmth of the production is immediate. From the opening 
            stabs of the title track, you're transported to a world of Wurlitzers and 
            gritty basslines. It's the kind of record that demands to be heard on vinyl, 
            through a pair of honest speakers.
        </p>

        <iframe src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/dQw4w9WgXcQ" title="YouTube video player" frameborder="0" allowfullscreen></iframe>
        
        <p>
            Ultimately, Francis isn't just mimicking the greats; he's adding to the lineage. 
            *Changes* is a bold statement of intent from an artist who clearly knows 
            where the soul is buried.
        </p>
    </section>

